# VelvetUi – Core Principles

## Overview

- SolidJS UI component library: `@jankrajewskiit/ui`
- Stack: SolidJS, TypeScript, CSS Modules, Vite
- Peers: `solid-js >=1.9`, `@solidjs/router >=0.15`

## Scope and Responsibilities

- Generic, app-agnostic components:
  - No domain/auth/business logic
  - No app-specific i18n logic – all copy via props
  - No data fetching or side-effectful API calls inside components

## Code Style and Cleanliness

- Self-documenting code:
  - No comments explaining obvious behavior
  - No commented-out code left in files
  - No `eslint-disable` (inline or file-level) unless explicitly requested
- Consistent TypeScript + SolidJS patterns (see `solidjs-tsx` rule for details)

## Project Structure (high level)

- `src/components/{category}/` – components grouped by category (m.in. `typography/`, `data-display/`, …)
- `src/hooks/` – reusable hooks
- `src/models/Props.ts` – shared `Props` model
- `src/theme/` – design tokens and theming
- `src/utils/` – shared utilities
- `src/index.ts` – library entry/exports
- `config/` – shared config packages and tooling
- `demo/` – demo application using the library
